// src/v4/extdeps/frameworks/react.dag
//
// Scope: React framework substrate — function components, Hook sites, effect
//         lifecycle triggers, client vs React-Server-Components module surfaces.
// Anchor (version pins — checkable L-2; extdeps declaration discipline):
//   React **19.1.0** (npm `react@19.1.0`): API surface frozen at
//   https://github.com/facebook/react/releases/tag/v19.1.0 and documented at
//   https://react.dev/reference/react (rolling site — the **semver tag** is
//   the L-2 fidelity authority; site drift = visible C1 edit to this header).
//   Mental model / composition: https://react.dev/learn
// Unifies: (per THESIS:188) framework spec = transport spec = interpreter
//         runtime where applicable. ONE substrate carrier per React program
//         slice; emission / ingest / eval lenses read distinct facts from the
//         same Node-shaped tree — extend THIS file, not parallel "emit-only"
//         mirrors.
//
// Owns:
//   - ReactModuleSurface = ReactClientModule | ReactServerComponentsModule
//     (closed — the exhaustive partition of **module-level** capability
//     surfaces React 19 documents for RSC vs client bundles; per TASKS.md
//     T-4.7 the fork is modeled HERE so hook-kind admissibility composes with
//     effect typing instead of bolting on a stringly "use client" annotation
//     layer — directive spelling lives in the boundary intern table, not the
//     kernel.)
//   - ReactFunctionComponent { surface, props_type_ref, root: Node }
//     — props are a TypeScript-shaped type at the language boundary; modeled as
//     an opaque `Symbol` name-reference into `v4.extdeps.languages.typescript`
//     (traceability only — no `import` edge until a ratified shared carrier
//     needs it; P2 single-authority).
//   - ReactHook { kind: ReactHookKind, dependencies: List<Node> }
//     — `dependencies` is the dependency-list spine hook consumers share
//     (empty for hooks without a dependency array such as `useState`;
//     ordered list matches React's array semantics).
//   - ReactHookKind = Builtin { hook: ReactBuiltinHook }
//     | Custom { implementation: Node }
//     (`Custom` is Node composition per Rules-of-Hooks — not a new hook kind;
//     feedback_nodes_are_nodes.)
//   - ReactBuiltinHook — the COMPLETE **react**-package stable hook set
//     enumerated at react.dev/reference/react for the pinned release (C1
//     closure — NO "…"; a missing hook at fill-time is a substrate-extension
//     STOP, not a silent open enum). Variant `UseApi` models the stable `use`
//     promise/resource reader (react.dev/reference/react/use) — spelling
//     `Use` alone is a reserved-shape hazard, so the carrier name is explicit.
//   - ReactComponentEffect { trigger: ReactEffectTrigger, effect_body: Node }
//     — `effect_body` is the full subtree for the effect callback + cleanup
//     composition (not a bare `Behavior` tag: a Behavior without children
//     cannot carry a program; INVARIANTS substrate uses `Node` as the ONE
//     recursive program carrier — reconciles the prior scaffold sketch).
//   - ReactEffectTrigger = Mount | Unmount | DependencyChange | EveryRender
//     (closed enum — **when** a modeled `ReactComponentEffect` runs relative
//     to the reconciler; maps to effect commit/cleanup scheduling facts in
//     the reference, not wall-clock time.)
//   - Rules-of-Hooks discipline — **lens-owned**: violations surface as
//     `std/diagnostic.dag` `Diagnostic` values raised by a react lens /
//     checker consuming this substrate (reason `Symbol` owned by that lens,
//     not enumerated here — THESIS §1.5 / diagnostic.dag schema).
//
// Consumes (traceability):
//   - std/node.dag: Node, Symbol (K-1 opaque identity for cross-module refs)
//   - std/collection.dag: List<T> for dependency lists
//   - extdeps/languages/typescript.dag: authoritative TS type graph for
//     `props_type_ref` resolution (traceability — no hard `import` until a
//     ratified shared carrier requires it)
//
// Owned ELSEWHERE (explicit deferrals — named triggers):
//   - JSX / TSX grammar, attribute/event emission, synthetic-event shapes —
//     bundled T-4 LanguageModel + emit lanes (TASKS.md T-4 B2-OMNI).
//   - Class components, Error boundaries, Suspense boundaries, concurrent
//     features beyond hook enumeration — grammar / library layers; not
//     duplicated here.
//   - Next.js / framework-specific directives (`"use client"`, routing) —
//     adjacent framework extdeps when operator-ratified; React core stops at
//     `ReactModuleSurface`.
//   - Per-hook algebra inhabitance (e.g. state semiring story) — composes with
//     std/algebra.dag when a D2-style resolver slice lands; same deferral shape
//     as language extdeps (no OrderedRing rows here pre-trigger).
//
// Status: T-4.7 modeled 2026-05-16 — structural carriers landed; grammar /
//   emit / per-hook inhabitance ride named ELSEWHERE owners.
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.extdeps.frameworks.react


import v4.std.node { Node, Symbol }
import v4.std.collection { List }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes
//
// REACT VS TYPESCRIPT. Props and hook operands are ECMAScript/TypeScript
// values at the language boundary — this file names them through `Node` trees
// (already lowered / embedded in the program graph) and `Symbol` references
// into the TS module graph for static props types. That keeps React's model
// from minting parallel string / Int carriers for TS facts (P2).
//
// RSC VS CLIENT. `ReactServerComponentsModule` values carry only the hook + DOM
// subsets React documents for server components; **which** hooks are illegal
// in a server module is enforced at the grammar / checker lens that reads
// `surface`, not by duplicating hook enums (single closed `ReactBuiltinHook`
// authority — admissibility is relative to `ReactModuleSurface`).
//
// EFFECT TRIGGERS. React's real engine interleaves commit + cleanup passes; the
// four-way `ReactEffectTrigger` sum is a modeling partition for **structural**
// scheduling obligations the testgen / coordination lenses read — not a
// runtime event log.


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactModuleSurface — client vs React Server Components module boundary
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: every endpoint / emit / capability lens reads
//      the same module-surface tag uniformly when composing React with
//      coordination.dag or TS emit.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: a `{ is_server: Bool }` proxy admits the
//      illegal (server ∧ client) simultaneous state and loses the named
//      partition react.dev uses for RSC vs client bundles.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: the distinction is an epistemic module boundary,
//      not an algebra inhabitant.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a compiled React module is **exactly one** of
//      these surfaces at the authority modeled here (mixed graphs compose at
//      the program / graph layer, not by fusing this tag).
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: not `F<X>` over a richer enumerable source;
//      the two surfaces are the irreducible React-19 module-capability story.
// Terminal: the closed binary partition for React 19 module-level capability.
type ReactModuleSurface
  = ReactClientModule
  | ReactServerComponentsModule


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactBuiltinHook — complete stable hook API of the `react` package (pinned
// React 19.1.0) per https://react.dev/reference/react .
//
// ORDERING NOTE. Variants follow the **react.dev left-nav / reference index**
// order for the Hooks section (`useState` … `use`) so external diff audits map
// mechanically to the doc table — not alphabetical, not dependency frequency.
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: every resolver / emit / cost consumer branches on
//      the built-in hook uniformly; shared classifier, not scattered string
//      tables (K-1-safe — no readable hook-name tokens in kernel logic).
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: `{ hook_id: Int }` replaces a closed 18-way
//      exhaustive sum with unbounded integers — illegal hook ids become
//      representable (P2).
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: each hook eventually composes with std/
//      effects + algebra carriers (state monoid, transition semiring, etc.) —
//      those are **inhabitance walks** owned ELSEWHERE; this enum stays the
//      closed API partition, not a collapse target into a single algebra.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a single hook call site selects EXACTLY ONE built-in
//      hook kind at a time — mutually exclusive alternatives.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: hooks are NOT `ReactHookOp<Width>` style
//      mechanical copies over an independent width enum (Practice 7); each
//      variant is its own named React API surface.
// Terminal: the closed eighteen-way stable hook classifier for React 19.1.0.
type ReactBuiltinHook
  = ReactUseState
  | ReactUseReducer
  | ReactUseContext
  | ReactUseRef
  | ReactUseImperativeHandle
  | ReactUseEffect
  | ReactUseLayoutEffect
  | ReactUseInsertionEffect
  | ReactUseMemo
  | ReactUseCallback
  | ReactUseTransition
  | ReactUseDeferredValue
  | ReactUseId
  | ReactUseSyncExternalStore
  | ReactUseDebugValue
  | ReactUseActionState
  | ReactUseOptimistic
  | ReactUseApi


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactHookKind — built-in vs custom-hook body
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: lowering + lint share one discriminant for hook
//      expansion vs user-authored hook functions.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: collapsing to `{ is_builtin: Bool, code: Node }`
//      admits "builtin with arbitrary implementation subtree" — contradicts
//      React's finite built-in set + Rules-of-Hooks composition for custom
//      hooks.
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: custom hooks reduce to Node composition of other
//      hooks — the `implementation` subtree is the monoid closure site, not a
//      second parallel enum.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a hook site is EITHER a named built-in OR a custom
//      Node body — never both simultaneously at the same call site.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: not a uniform `F<X>` / Practice-7 projection
//      over an independent index set; the two arms carry structurally different
//      payloads (`ReactBuiltinHook` vs `Node`).
// Terminal: the irreducible built-in vs custom hook partition.
type ReactHookKind
  = Builtin { hook: ReactBuiltinHook }
  | Custom { implementation: Node }


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactHook — hook kind + dependency list spine
//
// Conj record (no Practice-4 ledger).
type ReactHook {
  kind: ReactHookKind
  dependencies: List<Node>
}


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactEffectTrigger — structural scheduling obligations for effects
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: testgen / cost / coordination consumers read the
//      trigger uniformly when sequencing modeled effects.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: `{ phase_bits: Int }` reopens illegal trigger
//      combinations as representable states.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: triggers are reconciler-scheduling classes, not an
//      algebra carrier in std/.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: each modeled obligation is EXACTLY ONE trigger class
//      at the modeled site — mutually exclusive alternatives.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: not `F<Step>` over a declared step enum;
//      the four triggers name distinct reconciler obligations, not a uniform
//      copy of another set.
// Terminal: the closed four-way effect-trigger partition from the scaffold
// contract (TASKS.md T-4.7).
type ReactEffectTrigger
  = Mount
  | Unmount
  | DependencyChange
  | EveryRender


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactComponentEffect — effect callback subtree + trigger
//
// Conj record (no Practice-4 ledger).
type ReactComponentEffect {
  trigger: ReactEffectTrigger
  effect_body: Node
}


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactFunctionComponent — surface + props type ref + render tree root
//
// Conj record (no Practice-4 ledger).
type ReactFunctionComponent {
  surface: ReactModuleSurface
  props_type_ref: Symbol
  root: Node
}
